HST Office: Name Manager shows Excel's Value column (owner-approved Microsoft Office parity for beta.5).

The value is calculated when a row becomes visible, like the existing formula text: the result of the name,
or {...} for a block of cells. Paste Names shares the table and keeps its three columns. A Comment column
would need a new model property and a file round trip, so it is not included.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-sheets.py (name-manager).
